WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.380
You can hand a video to a coding agent and get a real edit back.

00:00:03.620 --> 00:00:06.540
What makes it work is a loop, not a lucky prompt.

00:00:07.940 --> 00:00:09.560
Step one is Transcribe.

00:00:10.210 --> 00:00:15.070
Every word gets a timestamp, so every graphic can land on the word it belongs to.

00:00:16.280 --> 00:00:17.640
Step two is Cut.

00:00:18.300 --> 00:00:22.780
Dead air, filler, and retakes come out, and every cut lands in silence.

00:00:24.250 --> 00:00:26.210
Step three is Plan the Beats.

00:00:26.630 --> 00:00:31.410
Each graphic gets a word to land on, a place on screen, and a reason to exist.

00:00:32.530 --> 00:00:38.290
Step four is Build. The agent writes the motion as a web page and renders it frame by frame.

00:00:39.160 --> 00:00:47.480
Step five is Verify. It measures the loudness, checks every cut and every card, and fixes what fails before you watch.

00:00:48.420 --> 00:00:55.580
Then the loop feeds itself. What you liked and what you didn't goes back into the skills, so the next edit starts smarter.

